IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 35 to 40 (regulations, model constitutions, the effect of the constitution, copies of it).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). s 36(2) (a power to prescribe different model constitutions) is machinery and is not encoded; s 40(3) is shown "[Omitted in 2006 Revised Edition]" and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- The model constitutions themselves are not in the Act: what a model says is a fact the caller supplies.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 35: the regulations for the company`

-- (1): "Subject to this section, a company's constitution must contain the regulations for the company."
-- "Subject to this section": once subsection (2) excludes the company the text is silent about (1) (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:5768 | 35.—(1) Subject to this section, a company’s constitution must
-- src:5769 | contain the regulations for the company.
@ref s 35(1) (src:5768-5769)
GIVEN `subsection (2) excludes the company from subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the constitution of the company must contain the regulations for the company` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) excludes the company from subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this section" -- once subsection (2) excludes the company, subsection (1) says nothing of it (fork line F-I18)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a company limited by shares that was incorporated before 3 January 2016."
-- src:5773 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a company limited by shares
-- src:5774 | that was incorporated before 3 January 2016.
@ref s 35(2) (src:5773-5774)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a company limited by shares that was incorporated before 3 January 2016" -- the subsection excludes that kind of company and says nothing of any other

-- (3): "Despite subsection (2), where immediately before 3 January 2016, regulations were in force for a company, whether the regulations were prescribed in the company's registered articles, or were applicable in lieu of or in addition to the company's registered articles by virtue of section 36(2) in force before that date,
-- such regulations are deemed to be the regulations for the company contained in the company's constitution for the purposes of subsection (1) until such time as the constitution of the company is amended to replace or amend those regulations."
-- "Until such time as": once the constitution is amended to replace or amend them, they are no longer deemed (JUST FALSE; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-I22).
-- src:5778 | (3) Despite subsection (2), where immediately before 3 January
-- src:5779 | 2016, regulations were in force for a company, whether the
-- src:5780 | regulations were prescribed in the company’s registered articles, or
-- src:5781 | were applicable in lieu of or in addition to the company’s registered
-- src:5782 | articles by virtue of section 36(2) in force before that date, such
-- src:5783 | regulations are deemed to be the regulations for the company
-- src:5784 | contained in the company’s constitution for the purposes of
-- src:5785 | subsection (1) until such time as the constitution of the company is
-- src:5786 | amended to replace or amend those regulations.
@ref s 35(3) (src:5778-5786)
GIVEN `regulations were in force for the company immediately before 3 January 2016, whether prescribed in its registered articles or applicable by virtue of section 36(2) in force before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company has been amended to replace or amend those regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3) the regulations are deemed to be the regulations for the company contained in its constitution` MEANS
    IF `regulations were in force for the company immediately before 3 January 2016, whether prescribed in its registered articles or applicable by virtue of section 36(2) in force before that date`
    THEN (IF `the constitution of the company has been amended to replace or amend those regulations`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are deemed to be the regulations ... until such time as the constitution of the company is amended to replace or amend those regulations" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it; fork line F-I22)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where immediately before 3 January 2016, regulations were in force for a company" -- regulations not then in force are outside the subsection

§ `Sections 36 to 38: model constitutions and companies limited by guarantee`

-- 36(1): "The Minister may prescribe model constitutions for — (a) private companies; and (b) companies limited by guarantee (called in this section and section 37 specified companies)."
-- Only the definition "specified companies" is encoded: the Minister's power to prescribe is machinery. It reads as a "called" definition: closed.
-- src:5792 | 36.—(1) The Minister may prescribe model constitutions for —
-- src:5794 | (a) private companies; and
-- src:5796 | (b) companies limited by guarantee,
-- src:5798 | (called in this section and section 37 specified companies).
@ref s 36(1) (src:5792-5798)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(1) the company is a specified company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` OR `s 4(1) "company limited by guarantee" the company is a company limited by guarantee` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "model constitutions for — (a) private companies; and (b) companies limited by guarantee (called in this section and section 37 specified companies)" (a "called" definition: closed, as the keel treats a "means" definition)

-- 37(1): "A specified company may adopt as its constitution the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which it belongs."
-- src:5809 | 37.—(1) A specified company may adopt as its constitution the
-- src:5810 | whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under
-- src:5811 | section 36(1) for the type of company to which it belongs.
@ref s 37(1) (src:5809-5811)
GIVEN `the company is a specified company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model constitution is the one prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1) the specified company may adopt the whole or any part of the model constitution as its constitution` MEANS
    IF `the company is a specified company` AND `the model constitution is the one prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A specified company may adopt as its constitution the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which it belongs" -- a permission whose subject or object is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (2): "A specified company may in its constitution adopt the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs by reference to the title of the model constitution."
-- src:5815 | (2) A specified company may in its constitution adopt the whole
-- src:5816 | model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs by
-- src:5817 | reference to the title of the model constitution.
@ref s 37(2) (src:5815-5817)
GIVEN `the company is a specified company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company adopts the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(2) the specified company may adopt the whole model constitution by reference to its title` MEANS
    IF `the company is a specified company` AND `the company adopts the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs` AND `the company adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A specified company may in its constitution adopt the whole model constitution ... by reference to the title of the model constitution" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

DECLARE `s 37(3) choice` IS ONE OF
    `s 37(3)(a) to adopt the model constitution as in force at the time of adoption`
    `s 37(3)(b) to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from time to time`
    `s 37(3) another choice`

-- (3): "Where a specified company adopts the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs, the specified company may choose — (a) to adopt the model constitution as in force at the time of adoption; or (b) to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from time to time ..."
-- src:5824 | (3) Where a specified company adopts the whole model
-- src:5825 | constitution for the type of company to which it belongs, the
-- src:5826 | specified company may choose —
-- src:5828 | (a) to adopt the model constitution as in force at the time of
-- src:5829 | adoption; or
-- src:5831 | (b) to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from
-- src:5832 | time to time, in which case the model constitution for the
-- src:5833 | type of company to which the specified company belongs
-- src:5834 | that is for the time being in force is, so far as applicable, the
-- src:5835 | constitution for that specified company.
@ref s 37(3) (src:5824-5835)
GIVEN `the specified company adopts the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      choice IS A `s 37(3) choice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(3) the specified company may choose` MEANS
    IF `the specified company adopts the whole model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs` AND (NOT (choice EQUALS `s 37(3) another choice`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a specified company adopts the whole model constitution ..., the specified company may choose — (a) ...; or (b) ..." -- a permission whose condition is not met, or a choice the subsection does not list; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (3)(b), second limb: "in which case the model constitution for the type of company to which the specified company belongs that is for the time being in force is, so far as applicable, the constitution for that specified company."
-- src:5831 | (b) to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from
-- src:5832 | time to time, in which case the model constitution for the
-- src:5833 | type of company to which the specified company belongs
-- src:5834 | that is for the time being in force is, so far as applicable, the
-- src:5835 | constitution for that specified company.
@ref s 37(3)(b) (src:5831-5835)
GIVEN `the specified company has chosen to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(3)(b) the model constitution for the time being in force is, so far as applicable, the constitution of the specified company` MEANS
    IF `the specified company has chosen to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from time to time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to adopt the model constitution as may be in force from time to time, in which case the model constitution ... for the time being in force is, so far as applicable, the constitution" (a status gated by "in which case": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I21)

-- (4): "A copy of the constitution of a specified company must be submitted to the Registrar, in accordance with section 19(1), where the specified company — (a) adopts only part of the model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs; (b) includes provisions additional to those in the model constitution; or (c) includes object clauses as part of its constitution."
-- A duty gated by "where": JUST FALSE where no limb holds (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21). Section 19(1) fixes the time and is outside this range, so no trace reaches BREACH.
-- src:5839 | (4) A copy of the constitution of a specified company must be
-- src:5840 | submitted to the Registrar, in accordance with section 19(1), where
-- src:5841 | the specified company —
-- src:5843 | (a) adopts only part of the model constitution for the type of
-- src:5844 | company to which it belongs;
-- src:5846 | (b) includes provisions additional to those in the model
-- src:5847 | constitution; or
-- src:5849 | (c) includes object clauses as part of its constitution.
@ref s 37(4) (src:5839-5849)
GIVEN `the company is a specified company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company adopts only part of the model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company includes provisions additional to those in the model constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company includes object clauses as part of its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(4) a copy of the constitution of the specified company must be submitted to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a specified company`
      AND (    `the company adopts only part of the model constitution for the type of company to which it belongs`
            OR `the company includes provisions additional to those in the model constitution`
            OR `the company includes object clauses as part of its constitution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the constitution of a specified company must be submitted to the Registrar ... where the specified company — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (a duty gated by "where": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

DECLARE `s 37(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 37(4) submit a copy of the constitution to the Registrar in accordance with section 19(1)`

-- src:5839 | (4) A copy of the constitution of a specified company must be
-- src:5840 | submitted to the Registrar, in accordance with section 19(1), where
-- src:5841 | the specified company —
-- src:5843 | (a) adopts only part of the model constitution for the type of
-- src:5844 | company to which it belongs;
-- src:5846 | (b) includes provisions additional to those in the model
-- src:5847 | constitution; or
-- src:5849 | (c) includes object clauses as part of its constitution.
@ref s 37(4) (src:5839-5849)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 37(4) act`
`s 37(4) the specified company must submit a copy of its constitution to the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 37(4) submit a copy of the constitution to the Registrar in accordance with section 19(1)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 37(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the specified company did not submit a copy of its constitution to the Registrar in accordance with section 19(1)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- 38(1): "In the case of a company limited by guarantee, every provision in the constitution or in any resolution of the company purporting to give any person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company, otherwise than as a member, is void."
-- src:5855 | 38.—(1) In the case of a company limited by guarantee, every
-- src:5856 | provision in the constitution or in any resolution of the company
-- src:5857 | purporting to give any person a right to participate in the divisible
-- src:5858 | profits of the company, otherwise than as a member, is void.
@ref s 38(1) (src:5855-5858)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the provision purports to give a person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company otherwise than as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1) the provision is void` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "company limited by guarantee" the company is a company limited by guarantee` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the provision purports to give a person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company otherwise than as a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company limited by guarantee, every provision ... purporting to give any person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company, otherwise than as a member, is void" -- the subsection avoids provisions of that kind in that kind of company and says nothing of any other (fork line F-I32; the earlier pass answers FALSE here)

-- (2): "For the purposes of the provisions of this Act relating to the constitution of a company limited by guarantee and of this section, every provision in the constitution or in any resolution of a company limited by guarantee purporting to divide the undertaking of the company into shares or interests is to be treated as a provision for a share capital even though the number of the shares or interests is not specified thereby."
-- src:5862 | (2) For the purposes of the provisions of this Act relating to the
-- src:5863 | constitution of a company limited by guarantee and of this section,
-- src:5864 | every provision in the constitution or in any resolution of a company
-- src:5865 | limited by guarantee purporting to divide the undertaking of the
-- src:5866 | company into shares or interests is to be treated as a provision for a
-- src:5867 | share capital even though the number of the shares or interests is not
-- src:5868 | specified thereby.
@ref s 38(2) (src:5862-5868)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the provision purports to divide the undertaking of the company into shares or interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(2) the provision is treated as a provision for a share capital` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "company limited by guarantee" the company is a company limited by guarantee` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the provision purports to divide the undertaking of the company into shares or interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every provision in the constitution or in any resolution of a company limited by guarantee purporting to divide the undertaking of the company into shares or interests is to be treated as a provision for a share capital" -- another provision, or another kind of company, is outside the subsection

§ `Sections 39 and 40: the effect of the constitution and copies of it`

-- (1): "Subject to this Act, the constitution of a company, when registered, binds the company and the members thereof to the same extent as if it respectively had been signed and sealed by each member and contained covenants on the part of each member to observe all the provisions of the constitution."
-- "Subject to this Act" points to the provisions of the Act that otherwise provide (NOTHING). "When registered": a status gated by "when", JUST FALSE before registration (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I21).
-- src:5877 | 39.—(1) Subject to this Act, the constitution of a company, when
-- src:5878 | registered, binds the company and the members thereof to the same
-- src:5879 | extent as if it respectively had been signed and sealed by each
-- src:5880 | member and contained covenants on the part of each member to
-- src:5881 | observe all the provisions of the constitution.
@ref s 39(1) (src:5877-5881)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the constitution binds the person to the same extent as if signed and sealed by each member` MEANS
    IF `this Act otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this Act" -- the other provision of the Act, not this subsection, says what binds
    ELSE (IF `the constitution of the company is registered`
          THEN (IF `the person is the company or a member of the company`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "binds the company and the members thereof" -- the subsection names no other person
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the constitution of a company, when registered, binds the company and the members thereof" (a status gated by "when": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I21)

-- (2): "All money payable by any member to the company under the constitution is a debt due from the member to the company."
-- src:5885 | (2) All money payable by any member to the company under the
-- src:5886 | constitution is a debt due from the member to the company.
@ref s 39(2) (src:5885-5886)
GIVEN `the money is payable by a member to the company under the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(2) the money is a debt due from the member to the company` MEANS
    IF `the money is payable by a member to the company under the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All money payable by any member to the company under the constitution is a debt due" -- money payable on another footing is outside the subsection

-- (3): "Despite anything in the constitution of a company, no member of the company, unless either before or after the alteration is made the member agrees in writing to be bound thereby, is bound by an alteration made in the constitution after the date on which the member became a member so far as the alteration requires the member to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by the member at the date on which the alteration is made
-- or in any way increases the member's liability as at that date to contribute to the share capital of or otherwise to pay money to the company."
-- Once the member has agreed in writing the "unless" is met and the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:5890 | As to effect of alterations on members who do not consent
-- src:5892 | (3) Despite anything in the constitution of a company, no member
-- src:5893 | of the company, unless either before or after the alteration is made the
-- src:5894 | member agrees in writing to be bound thereby, is bound by an
-- src:5895 | alteration made in the constitution after the date on which the member
-- src:5896 | became a member so far as the alteration requires the member to take
-- src:5897 | or subscribe for more shares than the number held by the member at
-- src:5898 | the date on which the alteration is made or in any way increases the
-- src:5899 | member’s liability as at that date to contribute to the share capital of
-- src:5900 | or otherwise to pay money to the company.
@ref s 39(3) (src:5890-5900)
GIVEN `the alteration was made after the date on which the member became a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration requires the member to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by the member at the date on which the alteration is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration in any way increases the member's liability as at that date to contribute to the share capital of or otherwise to pay money to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member agrees in writing, before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(3) the member is bound by the alteration` MEANS
    IF    `the alteration was made after the date on which the member became a member`
      AND (    `the alteration requires the member to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by the member at the date on which the alteration is made`
            OR `the alteration in any way increases the member's liability as at that date to contribute to the share capital of or otherwise to pay money to the company`)
    THEN (IF `the member agrees in writing, before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by it`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless either before or after the alteration is made the member agrees in writing to be bound thereby" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the member is bound (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no member of the company ... is bound by an alteration made in the constitution after the date on which the member became a member so far as the alteration requires the member to take or subscribe for more shares ... or in any way increases the member's liability"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as the alteration requires ... or in any way increases" -- another alteration, or one made before the member became a member, is outside the subsection

-- 40(1): "A company must, on being so required by any member, send to the member a copy of the constitution (if any) subject to payment of $5 or such lesser sum as is fixed by the directors."
-- The sum: $5, or the lesser sum the directors fix.
-- src:5906 | 40.—(1) A company must, on being so required by any member,
-- src:5907 | send to the member a copy of the constitution (if any) subject to
-- src:5908 | payment of $5 or such lesser sum as is fixed by the directors.
@ref s 40(1) (src:5906-5908)
GIVEN `the directors have fixed a sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the directors have fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(1) the sum the member must pay for a copy of the constitution` MEANS
    IF `the directors have fixed a sum` AND `the sum the directors have fixed` LESS THAN 5
    THEN `the sum the directors have fixed`
    ELSE 5

-- The duty is gated by the member's requirement, the company having a constitution ("(if any)") and payment of the sum: JUST FALSE where a gate fails (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I29).
-- src:5906 | 40.—(1) A company must, on being so required by any member,
-- src:5907 | send to the member a copy of the constitution (if any) subject to
-- src:5908 | payment of $5 or such lesser sum as is fixed by the directors.
@ref s 40(1) (src:5906-5908)
GIVEN `a member has required the company to send a copy of the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has paid the sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) the company must send the member a copy of the constitution` MEANS
    IF `a member has required the company to send a copy of the constitution` AND `the company has a constitution` AND `the member has paid the sum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, on being so required by any member, send to the member a copy of the constitution (if any) subject to payment of $5 or such lesser sum as is fixed by the directors" (a duty gated by the requirement, "(if any)" and payment: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I29)

DECLARE `s 40(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 40(1) send to the member a copy of the constitution`

-- No time is fixed, so no trace reaches BREACH.
-- src:5906 | 40.—(1) A company must, on being so required by any member,
-- src:5907 | send to the member a copy of the constitution (if any) subject to
-- src:5908 | payment of $5 or such lesser sum as is fixed by the directors.
@ref s 40(1) (src:5906-5908)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 40(1) act`
`s 40(1) the company must send a copy of the constitution to the member who requires it` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 40(1) send to the member a copy of the constitution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 40(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send the member a copy of the constitution when the member required it and paid the sum" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (2): "Where an alteration is made in the constitution of a company, a copy of the constitution must not be issued by the company after the date of alteration unless — (a) the copy is in accordance with the alteration; or (b) a copy of the order or resolution making the alteration is annexed to the copy of the constitution and the particular clauses affected are indicated."
-- A bar gated by "Where": JUST FALSE where the gate fails (fork line F-I21); once an "unless" limb is met the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:5912 | (2) Where an alteration is made in the constitution of a company, a
-- src:5913 | copy of the constitution must not be issued by the company after the
-- src:5914 | date of alteration unless —
-- src:5916 | (a) the copy is in accordance with the alteration; or
-- src:5918 | (b) a copy of the order or resolution making the alteration is
-- src:5919 | annexed to the copy of the constitution and the particular
-- src:5920 | clauses affected are indicated.
@ref s 40(2) (src:5912-5920)
GIVEN `an alteration is made in the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the alteration is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the company issues the copy of the constitution` IS A DATE
      `the copy is in accordance with the alteration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order or resolution making the alteration is annexed to the copy and the particular clauses affected are indicated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) the company must not issue the copy of the constitution` MEANS
    IF `an alteration is made in the constitution of the company` AND `the day the company issues the copy of the constitution` GREATER THAN `the day the alteration is made`
    THEN (IF `the copy is in accordance with the alteration` OR `a copy of the order or resolution making the alteration is annexed to the copy and the particular clauses affected are indicated`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless — (a) the copy is in accordance with the alteration; or (b) a copy of the order or resolution ... is annexed" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the company may issue the copy (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an alteration is made in the constitution of a company, a copy of the constitution must not be issued by the company after the date of alteration" (a bar gated by "Where" and "after the date of alteration": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (a) and (b); fork line F-I21)

-- (4): "If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence."
-- The subsection names no penalty (a general penalty provision elsewhere in the Act, outside this range, may apply): so no penalty function is written.
-- src:5931 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:5932 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:5933 | an offence.
@ref s 40(4) (src:5931-5933)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 40` AND `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-I10)
